# Real, current (non-deprecated) ArduPilot hardening -- the exact same
# two mechanisms already verified live against BlueBoat (see
# vehicle_twins/mass_resilient_blueboat/hardened.parm for the full
# verification notes). Carried over unmodified in value: both mechanisms
# are ArduPilot-parameter-level (GCS-link enforcement, EKF/GPS fusion
# behavior), not hull-specific, so they should transfer to CUSV's much
# larger hull unchanged -- but this is re-verified live against CUSV
# specifically in vehicle_twins/mass_resilient_cusv/README.md, not assumed
# just because it worked on a 30kg boat.
#
# GPS1_TYPE 14: switches the GPS driver to AP_GPS_MAV (external MAVLink
# GPS_INPUT), so GPS becomes just another sensor the EKF fuses and
# cross-checks against the real Gazebo-physics-derived IMU -- rather than
# GPS being embedded in the same JSON FDM feed the IMU is also derived
# from.
#
# MAV_GCS_SYSID 77 + MAV_OPTIONS 1 (bit 0 = GCS_SYSID_ENFORCE): only
# accepts GCS-privileged commands (arm, mode-change, RC-override) from
# sender id 77. An attacker using ArduPilot's plain default (255) gets
# rejected outright.
GPS1_TYPE 14
MAV_GCS_SYSID 77
MAV_OPTIONS 1
